WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
两辆车碰了一下。你会怎样描述刚才的速度？
Two cars collide. How would you describe their speed?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.000
“碰到”与“猛撞”，给同一段画面配了不同的词。
“Hit” and “smashed” put different words on the same footage.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000
洛夫特斯和帕尔默发现，提问用词影响速度估计。
Loftus and Palmer found that wording affected speed estimates.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.400
另一项实验里，研究者在看片一周后追问碎玻璃。
In a separate experiment, researchers asked about broken glass one week after viewing.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:30.000
片中没有碎玻璃。先前读到“猛撞”的人，更常回答看见了。
There was no broken glass. People who read “smashed” earlier reported seeing it more often.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.000
回忆会把原线索、后来的描述和推断拼到一起。
Recall can combine original cues, later descriptions, and inference.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.000
拼得完整的感觉，本身不能证明每个细节都准确。
A complete-feeling memory cannot prove each detail is accurate.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.700
元认知也包括监测自己的把握有多可靠。
Metacognition includes monitoring how reliable your confidence is.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:51.000
把“我很确定”与“记录支持”分别写下来。
Write down your confidence and the evidence separately.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.900
先独立记下你看到的，再核对当时的照片或记录。
Record what you saw before comparing it with a photo or record.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:01.000
有了核对的结果，下次才知道该给自己的把握打几折。
Checking gives you feedback for calibrating future confidence.
